WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.785 --> 00:00:07.230
- In India, poverty is so pervasive

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:08.820
that you can either decide

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.780
to forget about it or you
can decide to fight it.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:13.743
We can't ignore it.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.610
India has the world's
largest child population.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.260
More than 150 million children

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.620
in the age group of zero to
six years of age live in India.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.440
50% of them go to the
free government system.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.210
However, if you look at grade five

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.850
and learning outcomes,
we find that nearly half

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.650
of the kids in India are unable

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.300
to read a single paragraph

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.190 position:61%
or to do basic subtraction or division,

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.740 position:59%
we train them as unable to do anything

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:39.030
for their informal education

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.330
or even formal employment.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.230
My goal as a social entrepreneur

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.600
is to come up with
solutions and innovations

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.400 position:66%
that really change the fabric of the world

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.740
in a way that benefits
low-income populations

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.350
and populations that nobody
is building anything for.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:54.150
Essentially, we're trying
to change the social fabric

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.160
of the country and the
norms of the country,

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.470
those situations where low-income
parents who are majority

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.300 position:56%
of the population are actually going

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:03.060
to spend time every day
20 minutes on learning.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.020
This is a huge change.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.360
You're trying to basically
shift time use patterns

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:07.920
of a huge population

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.290
onto something that they've
not been doing earlier.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:13.021
And so I think that challenge
is what consumes us every day.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:24.120
So I was born to a family
of government officials.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.950
We lived in smaller
parts of India as well,

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.180
and we could see the poverty

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.610
and the lack of opportunities
that others faced.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:32.040
But I was lucky that I
was a middle class family

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.930
and got the best out of education.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:35.190
I think from early age,

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:36.960
we were cognizant of the privilege

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.670
that we've had in terms
of great education,

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.950 position:63%
the opportunities that that afforded us,

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:43.440
and on the flip side,
the lack of opportunity

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.720
that faces more than five crore,

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.280
or 50 million children today

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.623
in the zero to six age
group in the country.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:51.750
The more I thought about it

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:53.310
and the more over the last 10 years

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:55.020
that I've worked in the
social impact space,

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.640
I felt that the first six years

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.650 position:66%
are where most of your development happens

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:00.690
with your brain and your body.

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:02.790
We're an EdTech nonprofit working

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:05.100
to help one million
children in India so far

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.663
with early childhood education.

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:10.380 position:59%
Our short-term goal at Rocket Learning

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.570 position:66%
is to really comprehensively work together

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.220
to help children get up to speed.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:16.920
Rocket Learning's approach

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.950
is to create these dynamic
digital communities

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.410
of parents and preschool teachers

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:25.680
to empower them and inspire
them to be active participants

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.960 position:59%
and enablers in their child's journey.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:31.350
So Rocket Learning has created
70,000 WhatsApp groups,

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.720
which act as dynamic communities

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.940 position:66%
on which we are able to share some content

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.550
that is easy for children
to do in their own homes

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.440
or in their learning centers.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.273
You already are on WhatsApp,

00:02:41.273 --> 00:02:42.390
you're already using it

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:44.820
to send messages to your
family, et cetera, et cetera.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:47.520
And so through that, 70,000 groups

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.650 position:63%
and one million parents get our content.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.380
We're able then to send
back nudges and content.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:53.910
It's very personalized
for a particular user

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.860 position:66%
or a particular group, particular teacher.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.560
We have more than 2,000
audiovisual pieces,

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:00.060
worksheets, et cetera, et cetera

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:02.040 position:63%
that are then shared with the last mile,

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:03.030
with parents and teachers

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.100 position:66%
who can then use them in their daily life.

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:19.950
- [Narrator] The railways are shut,

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:21.450
the airlines will soon be shut.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.640
Interstate bus travel is all shut.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:24.810
There's a lot of unknowns

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.760 position:64%
about how this is gonna play out in India

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:30.123
and the honest truth is nobody
really knows at this point.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.700
For close to two years in India

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:33.690
and in fact in the world,

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.730
children did not come to schools.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.560
So most schooling actually
shifted to homeschooling

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:38.580
for those two years.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.890 position:56%
And so maybe the higher income child

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:42.360
didn't lose out on so much.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.820
They also had access to
online classes and so on.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:47.250
But low income children
living in rural parts

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:48.780 position:56%
of the world were not able to access

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:50.280
any sort of online education.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.980
For the most part, that's
where our programs,

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.750 position:66%
following aging parents through technology

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.520
actually came into being.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.230
It's not rocket science honestly

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:00.090 position:58%
to teach kids the basic fundamentals.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.130
You just need to be able
to give some information

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.090
to the right person.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.876
One is parents of children,
low income parents.

00:04:05.876 --> 00:04:07.620
Secondly, we saw

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:10.860
that there are these 1.3
million Anganwadi workers

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:11.693
across the country,

00:04:11.693 --> 00:04:14.280
daycare workers paid by
government, all female.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:16.140 position:56%
They feel that they can be educators

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:17.700 position:66%
and that they should be recognized as such

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.110 position:64%
and they also feel that they need support

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:20.832 position:61%
to do a better job in their classrooms.

00:04:26.763 --> 00:04:28.320
Over the last few years,

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:30.360 position:64%
we've been lucky to see phenomenal impact

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:33.570
on the children, parents
and preschool teachers

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:35.820
who've been a part of the program.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:37.470
We've seen that for parents

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:39.450 position:64%
that is very significant behavior change.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:40.890 position:56%
Parents who're a part of our program

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:43.260
are actually engaging
twice the number of time,

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:44.093
the number of days

00:04:44.093 --> 00:04:46.830
as counterparts who are
not part of the program.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:48.270
They spend a lot more
time with their children,

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:50.250
they're a lot more confident
in their abilities,

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:51.390
and for children themselves,

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.130 position:66%
we see that they are actually school ready

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:54.900
and life ready by the age of six

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:56.520 position:56%
if they've gone through the program.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:00.480
Their scores on tests
improved by 30% or more

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:03.270
but more importantly, they
actually shifted to the top 1/3

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:04.680
of what they would have been

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:06.870 position:59%
if they were not part of this program.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:07.763
Even beyond academic skills,

00:05:07.763 --> 00:05:10.020 position:63%
I think the most visible signs of impact

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:11.160
are when I go to the field

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:14.490 position:66%
and talk to parents and Anganwadi workers.

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:15.660
And they tell me that children

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.220 position:66%
are not afraid of going to school anymore,

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:18.330
they're not running away.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.830
They want to go to the center.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:22.140
They're looking forward to these
playful learning activities

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:23.910 position:58%
as opposed to running away from them.

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:25.350 position:59%
They're confident in what they can do,

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:27.030
they don't mind getting
up in front of a group,

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.160 position:61%
and showcasing what they are able to do

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.420
and they have more self-control,

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:32.620
and ability to interact
with others as well.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:34.890
I think in that way,

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:37.560 position:64%
if you go and see some of these children,

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:40.020
really see them in a
very different trajectory

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.793
from what they were on otherwise.

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:45.870
There have been so many times

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:47.430 position:64%
when I thought that we've bitten off more

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:48.263
than we can chew.

00:05:48.263 --> 00:05:50.310 position:58%
That we're attempting the impossible.

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:51.390
And in fact, a lot of the ecosystem

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:52.350
has told us this as well,

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.570 position:58%
that why you're working with parents?

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:55.830 position:56%
How are they going to make a change?

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.390 position:64%
How are you using technology in a country

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.830
that often doesn't have any?

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.990
But then luckily, it's
always been counterbalanced

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:02.370
by the community of users

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:05.100
that we've had who've told
us in no uncertain terms

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:06.990 position:61%
that what you're doing is helpful to us

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:09.960
and we want you to
continue working with us.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.460
The most significant part

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:14.430
about our success as the
Rocket Learning organization

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.410 position:59%
has been the fact that we've been able

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:19.110
to get a lot of talented
vision-oriented people

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:19.943
right from the beginning

00:06:19.943 --> 00:06:22.273
who work together without any ego,

00:06:22.273 --> 00:06:24.973
all with the single-minded
focus to solve the problem.

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:28.740
I've been incredibly fortunate
in my personal journey

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.110
to have family members, parents,

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:33.570 position:64%
my spouse, siblings who have been willing

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.160
to support whatever I do

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.840
and in fact, who don't
think it's a step down

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:37.950
to go into social entrepreneurship

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:39.090
from a corporate career.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:40.260
The thing that is the best thing

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:41.790
that I could be doing
and they're proud of me

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:42.720
for doing that.

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:44.460 position:58%
And it takes away all pressure on you

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:46.200
to follow your dreams.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:47.400
A lot of my personal journey

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:50.190
has been driven by folks
who have supported me

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:51.023
and they've known

00:06:51.023 --> 00:06:52.620
that I'm not gonna be
financially as successful

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:54.000
as many of my peers.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.290
They've thought whatever I'm doing

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:56.910 position:63%
is the best thing that I could be doing,

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:57.867
and that I'll change the world

00:06:57.867 --> 00:07:00.117
and that's really been
a huge support for me.

